<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/beijing" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beijing.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-6">6 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Britain recognises the People's Republic of China</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The United Kingdom became the first major Western power to recognise <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a>'s communist government in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>. The decision, partly aimed at protecting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a>, split <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> from US policy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-26">26 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">India becomes a republic under its new constitution</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-india">Constitution of India</a> came into force and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajendra-prasad">Rajendra Prasad</a> became the first President, replacing the British monarch as head of state. The day is celebrated as Republic Day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-9">9 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Joseph McCarthy claims to have a list of communists in the State Department</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In a speech at Wheeling, West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wisconsin">Wisconsin</a> senator said he held a list of 205 communists in the State <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">Department</a>. The charge launched years of anti-communist investigations.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-9">9 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Robert Schuman proposes pooling Europe's coal and steel</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>'s foreign minister proposed placing French and German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> under a common authority, making war between them 'materially impossible'. It led to the European Coal and Steel Community.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">Steel</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-25">25 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">North Korea invades South Korea</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">North Korean troops crossed the 38th parallel in force. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korean-war">Korean War</a> drew in UN forces and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and ended in a 1953 armistice near the original line.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-27">27 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">UN Security Council calls on members to defend South Korea</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Resolution 83 recommended that members help <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a> repel the North's attack. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> was boycotting the Council and could not veto it.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-15">15 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">UN forces land at Inchon</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">US Marines led General MacArthur's amphibious landing at Inchon, far behind North Korean lines. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seoul">Seoul</a> was retaken within two weeks and the North Korean army collapsed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chamdo">Battle of Chamdo</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Chamdo was fought in October 1950 in eastern Tibet, when the People's Liberation Army crossed the Jinsha River and defeated the Tibetan army around the town of Chamdo, capturing the regional governor Ngapoi Ngawang Jigme.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/briggs-plan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/briggs-plan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/briggs-plan">Briggs Plan</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Briggs Plan was the British strategy against the communist insurgency in Malaya devised in 1950 by Lieutenant-General Sir Harold Briggs, the director of operations during the Malayan Emergency.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-route-coloniale-4" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-route-coloniale-4.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-route-coloniale-4">Battle of Route Coloniale 4</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Route Coloniale 4 was a series of engagements in September and October 1950 along the road linking French frontier posts near the Chinese border in northern Vietnam.</p></div></li></ol></section>
